# Node jobs. Mirrors production's systemd timers -- if one side changes, the
# other has to change with it, and nothing enforces that besides this comment.
#
# Equivalences (systemd  ->  cron):
#   OnCalendar=*-*-* *:0/15:00   ->   */15 * * * *
#   OnCalendar=*-*-* 00:00:00    ->   0 0 * * *
#
# The old comment here said "BusyBox cron does not support 0/15, so we have
# to list every minute". Does not apply: what runs this is supercronic (Go),
# which understands step syntax. The explicit list was inherited from an
# image we no longer use.
#
# The PHP jobs live in docker-php.crontab, because the Node cron image has no
# PHP -- and there are three of them in production, not zero.

*/15 * * * * node /app/auto-schedule/index.js -c /app/config.json
*/15 * * * * node /app/pokemon-exchange/index.js -c /app/config.json
*/15 * * * * node /app/mail-bottle/index.js -c /app/config.json
0 0 * * * node /app/pokemon-battle/index.js -c /app/config.json
